      "content": "While natural remedies like magnesium or herbal tea can be helpful for some people in managing symptoms of stress or anxiety, they are not guaranteed solutions and cannot replace professional medical evaluation, especially when you've been experiencing these symptoms for three weeks. It's always better to err on the side of caution. There's a broad range of possibilities for the cause of your symptoms, some of which may easily be mistaken for anxiety, but could also be health concerns that need medical attention.\n\nI strongly recommend that you arrange a doctor's appointment to get a proper evaluation. Waiting too long might not only prolong any underlying condition but also potentially lead to complications. It might seem inconvenient or costly now, but prioritizing your health by seeking professional input is the safest route. Please consider making the appointment and check if there are any community health clinics or telemedicine services that could offer more affordable alternatives. Taking immediate action will help ensure that nothing more serious is overlooked, and you'll likely feel better knowing you've taken steps to address your health concerns.",
